sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design (agreed with Nick step by step, 2026-11-07): a task start copies the host's base VM snapshot and gives the copy a fixed slot identity. A slot is only an identity (shark-tvm-3: Node, WireGuard key and hub peer, host key, agent secret), kept by the Gateway; no slot VM waits ready.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: tasks:provision
  %% kind: tasks.provision
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane VM icon=server pill=task VM tone=purple
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant H as Task VM host<br/>Incus over ssh
  participant VM as Task VM<br/>shark-tvm-3
  Note over GW: Claim a slot identity<br/>mint the claim's keys
  %%> Started by:
  %%> - `tasks:provision` for a todo group, from proof CI or feature work
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the group holds the free identity `shark-tvm-3`; its Node, WireGuard peer, host key and agent secret already exist
  %%> - the Gateway mints the claim's Pi token and model key into the vault; about 1 s
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-tasks-provision
  SW->>H: Create and start the VM<br/>copy of the base snapshot
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one host exec: `incus copy` of the base VM's recorded snapshot and a clone of its seed snapshot (ZFS clones), `incus start`, then the slot identity and the claim's keys from the vault on stdin and the services that use them
  %%> - the containers start by themselves (`boot.autostart`) and already hold the proof Swamp Club key of the base
  %%> - beside it, the claim's model key is registered with the model router
  SW->>VM: Converge and branch<br/>the release's converge
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the same Ansible converge as the release refresh; with no delta every part is skipped, and it catches up a small delta when main moved since the last release
  %%> - then the new task branch on the checkout
  %%> - it waits for no nested service
  SW->>VM: Check ready<br/>one exec
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - what a task needs: the agent, Pi, the tunnel and the three containers running; Swamp's `assert` decides
  alt the run passes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>ready
    Note over GW: Record the VM ready<br/>target about 30 s
  else a step failed
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - the VM and its seed clone are deleted, the claim's keys revoked, the identity freed
  end
